  "_manifest_sha256_note": "sha256 of manifest.json's BYTES, in the recorder's prefixed form. This is the value §22.8.9 calls `base_dressing` -- the digest a pin file names as the dressing its author looked at -- and it is the SAME NUMBER as the `manifest.json` row in `files` above, deliberately carried twice because the two are read for different questions: `files` answers *did the transport deliver these bytes*, and this answers *which dressing does an authored pin file claim*. tools/emit_pins.py resolves it against a committed data/dressing/*/manifest.json at HEAD, and magisteria's tests/data/da9_emitted_pins.json carries exactly this value ONCE §25 backlog 739's re-emission is committed -- until then that fixture still names the superseded 5530e5b3..., and the client's emission (magisteria-patches/client-739/da9_emitted_pins.json, sha256 ec2792a7...) is what carries this one. Stated as a condition rather than a fact because the two repositories land at different moments and the sentence was true-by-the-time-you-read-it last time only by luck.",
  "dressing_sha256": "sha256:d3da07b0800b74d2d18dcd073b2c708b56b62c5cc865c3fd7304b0735966f880",
  "_dressing_sha256_note": "THE DRESSING'S IDENTITY, AND A DIFFERENT DOMAIN FROM THE FIELD ABOVE -- which is why §23.1745 exists and why both are carried here under their own names. This is sha256 over the four files in a FIXED ORDER -- manifest.json, tiles.jsonl, features.jsonl, routes.jsonl -- each contributing `name` + NUL + `len(bytes)` as decimal + NUL + `bytes`. The name and length prefixes are load-bearing, not decoration: plain concatenation of the same four files in the same order gives 38bad9c571ab13ea41b4d7b8ce81202305db0de6e1f4ebe88c61cc4fd941a8ad instead (recomputed at this re-cut: the counterexample is only a counterexample if it is this dressing's). This is the value owner ruling 2140 names in accepting the regenerated dressing, and `data/dressing/da6_readout.json` records under its `dressings` map at the `data/dressing/da6-compact` key -- both read back at this re-cut rather than assumed. BOTH DIGESTS ABOVE WERE COMPUTED FROM THE COMMITTED BYTES AND NEITHER WAS COPIED FROM A SIMULATION-REPO FILE; agreeing with the recorded values afterwards is the check, not the source.",
  "_what_this_pin_deliberately_does_not_carry": "ANY STRING FROM THE MANIFEST. The manifest's free text and tokens are the simulation's to hold and not this tree's to republish (decision 973, with the manifest's prose read and reported before these bytes were staged, per 2130 Q1): so no `generated_by`, no `record.path`, no `readings`, no `master_seed`, no settlement or plant identifiers -- this pin carries digests, byte counts and a commit, and nothing else. `generated_by` IS present in assets/terrain/PIN, so its absence here is a decision and not an omission. `source.path` above is not an exception: it is where this pin read the bytes, which every pin in this repo declares, and not a field copied out of the artefact.",
