    "_why_fetched_is_NOT_decision_948": "EVERY FILE HERE IS UNDER 948's LINE AND THE FOUR TOGETHER ARE OVER IT, AND NEITHER FACT IS WHY THEY ARE FETCHED. Measured at this re-cut: the largest is tiles.jsonl at 9,460,926 bytes, under the 10,485,760-byte threshold, while the four total 11,721,773, over it. Before the regeneration the largest was 7,273,940 and the total 7,640,642, under it on both readings -- so a reader who checked the sizes last time and checks them now gets a different answer to the same question, which is why the measurement is written out rather than left to be redone. THIS PIN TAKES NO POSITION ON WHETHER 948 READS PER FILE OR PER ARTEFACT. That is not ruled, and it does not change what happens here: these bytes are fetched either way. The reason is decision 2129 on decision 973's question -- 948's threshold partitions HOW A LARGE ARTEFACT IS HOSTED, not WHETHER A PUBLIC TREE MAY CARRY A SIMULATION ARTEFACT'S CONTENT. The owner answered that second question *\"Fetched by PIN\"*, rejecting both a reduced export and not publishing at all, and that answer holds whatever the size. `threshold_bytes` is deliberately absent: it is assets/fixture/PIN's field, nothing in the fetcher reads it, and here it would assert the wrong reason.",
